 Final Numbers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep ; Chart: Dan Primack/Axios SpaceX has held talks with EchoStar about either acquiring Boost Mobile or accessing its wireless network, according to The Washington Post .

 This reportedly comes after Elon Musk's company was rebuffed for network access by AT&amp;T, T-Mobile, and Verizon. That would make Boost — which relies on AT&amp;T and T-Mobile — a workaround solution that may come with litigation risk. SpaceX last year agreed to pay around $17 billion to buy wireless spectrum from EchoStar, although the deal has not yet closed.

 
 
